{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SubstratePeriodsIndependent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SubstratePeriodsIndependent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Complex.FiniteDimensional"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SubstratePeriods.periods_card_eq_finrank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SubstratePeriods.periods_card_eq_finrank","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SubstratePeriodsIndependent.lean#L77-L85","doc":"The two periods span `ℂ` over `ℝ`: being `ℝ`-independent and of cardinality\n`2 = finrank ℝ ℂ`, they form a `Basis (Fin 2) ℝ ℂ` — the exact input\n`DoublyPeriodicLiouville.ratio_const_of_doublyPeriodic` consumes. The `Basis`\nfollows from `periods_linearIndependent` by the standard \"independent family of\nsize `finrank` is a basis\" constructor; only the independence content is proved\nhere (it is the load-bearing fact — the basis is its mechanical corollary). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SubstratePeriods.periods_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SubstratePeriods.periods_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SubstratePeriodsIndependent.lean#L37-L75","doc":"**The two Faddeev–Volkov periods are `ℝ`-linearly independent** whenever\n`Im(b²) ≠ 0`. Proof: an `ℝ`-relation `s•(ib) + t•(i/b) = 0` factors through `I`\nand, after clearing `b`, gives `s·b² + t = 0`; taking imaginary parts (`t` real)\nyields `s·Im(b²) = 0`, so `s = 0`, whence `t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}